==Spanish==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|es|América|ano}}

===Pronunciation===
{{es-IPA}}
* {{audio|es|LL-Q1321 (spa)-Millars-americano.wav|Audio (Spain)}}
* {{rhymes|es|ano|s=5}}

===Adjective===
{{es-adj}}

# of the [[America]]s
# {{lb|es|proscribed}} of the [[United States]]

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m|f=americana}}

# [[American]] (a native of the [[America]]s)
# {{lb|es|proscribed}} American (a native of the [[United States]])
# someone who became rich in the Americas and returned to his country
# {{lb|es|Philippines|historical|obsolete}} person born and/or raised in [[Spanish America]] who [[immigrate]]d or [[visited]] the [[w:Captaincy General of the Philippines|Spanish Colonial Philippines]] or [[w:Spanish East Indies|Spanish East Indies]] in general.
#: {{syn|es|criollo}}
#: {{coordinate terms|es|peninsular|insular|filipino|filipina}}
# {{lb|es|US|Philippines}} person born and/or raised in the [[United States]].

====Usage notes====
* Definition 1 is the common meaning.
* Definition 2 is more modern and borrowed from English. It is more commonly used in Spain than in the Americas, although its use is discouraged on both regions.
* Definition 3 is very rarely used, the term [[indiano]] being more common.
* It is primarily in the United States where '''americano''' is currently used in reference to the United States. Otherwise, in Spanish '''americano''' is always used in reference to the Americas. For the United States (country) in particular, the more precise term is {{m|es|estadounidense}}.
* The usage of the term {{m|es|norteamericano}} in reference to the United States is not strictly speaking correct, as this term technically refers to North America (which in Spanish it is restricted to Canada, the United States and Mexico); however, it is very commonly used in reference to the U.S. on formal writing and in academia.

In the [[Philippines]] during [[w:History of the Philippines (1565–1898)|Spanish Colonial Times]], {{coordinate terms|es|[[criollo]] / [[americano]]|t=[[Spaniard]] born and/or raised in the [[Spanish]] [[Americas]], such as [[Mexico]]}}.<br>In the [[Philippines]] during [[w:History of the Philippines (1565–1898)|Spanish Colonial Times]], {{coordinate terms|es|insular|t=[[Spaniard]] born and/or raised in the [[Philippines]]}}.<br>In [[Spain]] and [[Spanish America]] during [[w:History of the Philippines (1565–1898)|Spanish Colonial Times]] in the [[Philippines]], {{coordinate terms|es|[[filipino]] / [[filipina]]|t=[[Spaniard]] born and/or raised in the [[Philippines]]}}.

